ith no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Tennessee carries a partisan lean of about fourteen points toward Republicans, making it one of the stronger GOP states on the presidential map. The 2028 contest is an open race, with no incumbent on the ballot because the sitting president is term-limited. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available for this race yet, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisan fundamentals.\n\nStatewide Republican strength is the dominant feature here; the 2026 governor's race, settled through a contested primary between Blackburn and Rose, underscores the party's firm hold on Tennessee politics. A Democratic breakthrough would require a substantial national shift well beyond anything currently measured. The expectation is a comfortable Republican win, with wide uncertainty until race-specific polling appears.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0961, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1038, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1086, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0965, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1008, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1057, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.104, "margin": -14.0}, {"date":